// Ways in from outside the program.
//
// The analyzed beams are not the whole system: a library's users, the
// runtime and the compiler call into it too. Rules ask, of a function,
// whether a caller the program does not show can call it, and they asked
// it five ways (failure's exposed roots, unsafe_input's outside_api,
// races' table_from_outside and open_source, concurrency's open_entry).
// Two questions stand behind them, and are named here:
//
// - api_export(f): a caller outside the program may call f. Every
//   exported function but those the compiler calls or makes: a macro
//   (`MACRO-name`, run at compile time with the code that uses it), and
//   the reflection a module is compiled with (`__info__/1`,
//   `module_info/0,1`, `__struct__`, `__impl__`, `__schema__` and the
//   other `__name__` functions of no arguments a `use` defines for its
//   library to read; reflection/2).
//   A function the program also calls is still its users' API (an Ecto
//   type's cast/1). Callbacks are exported, and the runtime calls them:
//   a rule for which the runtime's call is not an outside party's leaves
//   them out itself (unsafe_input's runtime_callback), and one for which
//   it is — failure's guard, which no try of the program's covers —
//   keeps them.
// - library_face(f): an api_export of a module no other module of the
//   program calls into — the program is that module's client nowhere, so
//   its users are the ones who call it. A module other modules of the
//   program call is one whose callers are in view: an export of it none
//   of them calls is unused (the tests, not in the beams, may call it),
//   not a way in. nerves_hub_web's CLISessionCache is the shape: Accounts
//   calls its get_and_update/2 and get/1, and only the tests call its
//   clear/0. The same module in a library nothing calls into is all API,
//   clear/0 included. It misses a module a library both calls itself and
//   hands its users, through a function the library never calls (quiet).
//   open_entry(f) is a library_face nothing in the program calls.
//
// Requires imports.dl.

.decl api_export(func: symbol)

api_export(f) :-
  function_def(f, _, n, a, 1),
  !match("MACRO-.*", n),
  !reflection(n, a),
  n != "module_info".

// The reflection a module is compiled with, which takes no outside data:
// any `__name__` function of no arguments (`__routes__/0`, `__live__/0`),
// and the compiler's and Ecto's lookups by a key of their own. A
// `__name__` function that takes arguments is otherwise a way in like
// any export: Phoenix's `__match_route__/3` takes the request's path.
.decl reflection(name: symbol, arity: number)

reflection(n, 0) :- function_def(_, _, n, 0, 1), match("__.*__", n).
reflection("__info__", 1).
reflection("__struct__", 1).
reflection("__impl__", 1).
reflection("__protocol__", 1).
reflection("__schema__", 1).
reflection("__schema__", 2).
reflection("__deriving__", 3).

// A module some other module of the program calls into.
.decl called_by_other_module(mod: symbol)

called_by_other_module(m) :-
  call_edge(c, g),
  function_def(g, m, _, _, _),
  function_def(c, cm, _, _, _),
  cm != m.

.decl library_face(func: symbol)

library_face(f) :-
  api_export(f),
  function_def(f, m, _, _, _),
  !called_by_other_module(m).

.decl open_entry(func: symbol)

open_entry(f) :- library_face(f), !call_edge(_, f).
